    {
      "id": "a76ab6ecd0869c80909985a57cafaf109f6e7c7b",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2015967764,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Current implementation is now to use GQueue, but then to cheat while iterating all members in order (by casting the private GList member out to iterate over) - otherwise g_queue_peek_nth() is a linear search (albeit starting from the shortest end).  The proper way with GQueue would be to use g_queue_foreach(), and define functions to call back, but that would have been cumbersome ( * )\n\nAccording to profiles, the first method (GSList + counter) speeded my capture up by 3.7%, whereas current code is 3.1%.  Likely due to chasing pointers *and* incrementing a counter variable for the (3) places where we need to walk the list in-order.\n\n( * ) as well as the overhead of calling the functions for each item, there would be the awkwardness of bundling up data into single void* arg and unpacking it inside the callback function..\n\nOpinions welcome.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/030414c33f619ee28811cd9c073802ef2267d160ab2744eb8427bd49af4c7998?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/martin.r.mathieson"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-07-25T12:52:25.035Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-07-25T13:10:29.536Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 317248448,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
